3. Right to public services .– (1) Subject to the provisions of the Act, every 
eligible person shall have a right to public services. 
(2) The right conferred under subsection (1) shall include the right to: 
(a) have access to the public service; 
(b) receive the public service within a specified time limit; 
(c) receive the public service in a transparent manner; 
(d) demand performance of duties and functions by the designated 
officers in accordance with the provisions of the Act;  
(e) hold the concerned designated officer account able for any 
service deficiency in the public service; and 
